# arms/adult/pose/woman_r: the woman's right arm in the postures (POSES-B, P2b wave 2): sleeve, bracer, hand
# (regions: U upper arm, F forearm, C cuff (the bracer), H hand). The posture keys (clips/postures.clip names them; GARB
# sleeves that follow the arm channels draw the same keys):
#   hold      the hand before the belly (a mug at rest, a bowl, a book, the drum's beat, the strum)
#   mouth     the hand at the mouth (drinking, eating, the flute)
#   raise     straight up over the head (a toast, the lamp pole, children at tag)
#   wave      the forearm up beside the head, the open hand (wave2: tilted out; the wave's other beat)
#   pray      the hands joined at the chest
#   reach     forward at the chest (a bowl held out, the reins, the rod, the oars' reach)
#   pull      the elbow back, the hand at the side (the oars' pull)
#   high      a tool raised over the shoulder (the hammer up, the axe up, the hoe up)
#   low       a tool struck down before the feet (the hammer on the anvil, the axe in the block, the hoe in the soil)
#   shoulder  the hand on the shoulder (a sack carried)
#   knee      the hand on the knee (kneeling, cross-legged)
# The front and back views draw both arms as near arms; facing right this arm is the near one, facing left the far one
# (behind the body: only what shows past it). Views whose hand comes before the face sit on the ears layer. `grip` marks
# where a prop's grip goes (maps/held/props: the prop is anchored there; its view picks a layer under the arm so the
# hand covers the grip, or over it where the prop comes before the face).
use person woman
body woman
role arms std
layer armNear
anchor shoulderR
keys armR
side R

